course: dictionary
lesson: 9265
title: Southwest: a direction and a place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Southwest is the direction halfway between south and west. On a compass it sits in the middle of S and W, and on maps it is short for SW. You can build the word from two parts: south + west = southwest.
explain: The southwest of a country is the part that lies in that direction. «In the dry Southwest the Ancestral Puebloans built houses of stone and adobe in cliffs and canyons.» The capital S shows it is a named region, and the word dry is a clue that this area is hot and dry.
explain: Southwest can also tell you where a wind comes from. A southwest wind blows from the southwest. Look for phrases like «to the southwest» and «south-west of» to find where something is on a map.
fact: Southwest is one of the eight main compass points, and it is written SW.
fact: On a compass, southwest is halfway between south and west, at 225 degrees from north.
fact: Southwest can be a noun («the southwest»), an adjective («southwest winds») or an adverb («to fly southwest»).
fact: Southwest is also written as south-west, with a hyphen.
fact: The Southwest of the USA includes states such as Arizona, Nevada and southern California, which have hot, dry deserts.
exercise: On a compass, which direction is halfway between south and west? | Southeast | Northeast | Northwest | *Southwest
exercise: A southwest wind blows from which direction? | From the north | *From the southwest | From the east | From the south-east
exercise: «The hot dry deserts of the Southwest in Arizona, Nevada and southern California» names which state? | Scotland | Maine | *Arizona | Wales
test: What is the short way to write southwest on a map? | *SW | NW | NS | SE
test: On a compass, how many degrees from north is southwest? | 270 | 180 | *225 | 90
exam: Which phrase tells you a place is in the direction halfway between south and west? | Under the sea | *To the southwest | In the north-east | Across the river
